WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.533
Week 29: Relative Clauses and Unknown Referents. define a requirement identify known and unknown people or things connect complex information

2
00:00:10.533 --> 00:00:19.529
Form and meaning. Relative pronouns; indicative versus subjunctive in adjective clauses; lo que, quien, el que, and cuyo.

3
00:00:19.529 --> 00:00:48.689
Model set. Buscamos a alguien que tenga experiencia. Conozco a la persona que dirige el proyecto. Necesito un lugar que esté cerca del metro. Eso es lo que me preocupa. La autora, cuyo libro ganó el premio, dará una charla. We are looking for someone who has experience. I know the person who directs the project. I need a place that is near the subway. That is what worries me. The author whose book won the prize will give a talk.

4
00:00:48.689 --> 00:00:58.968
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:13.365
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: define a requirement; identify known and unknown people or things; connect complex information. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:13.365 --> 00:01:43.249
Model language. Buscamos a alguien que tenga experiencia. — We are looking for someone who has experience. Conozco a la persona que dirige el proyecto. — I know the person who directs the project. Necesito un lugar que esté cerca del metro. — I need a place that is near the subway. Eso es lo que me preocupa. — That is what worries me. La autora, cuyo libro ganó el premio, dará una charla. — The author whose book won the prize will give a talk.

7
00:01:43.249 --> 00:01:53.254
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
